laurel 2989: the kernel path of a thread stuck on a silent CPU, read from another CPU; both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/watchdog.md section 10.

[V 2026-11-03 18:47:43, kernel c68eeb19c9] The third line of 2988 settled the kind of stall: CPU 5 was in the kernel on a Unix system call (madvise, by
the dyld slide of the line) for 19 s with interrupts off, its last interrupt taken at the enable in ml_set_interrupts_enabled. What that call does on
the CPU is the next question, and no debugger exists here. Three more lines, all reads by copies that cannot fault: the frame chain from the fp the
CPU's last interrupt found (sleh_irq passes it, post/9018; a spin in a leaf keeps its callers), every pointer into kernel text on the thread's kernel
stack (deepest first), and the thread's saved user registers (x16 = the system call number, x0-x3, sp, lr, pc). iOS 16: the fp line says none.

